5,Khün language - Detailed Pedia,https://www.detailedpedia.com/wiki-Khün_language,"The Khün varieties share 93% to 100% lexical similarity. Khun is closely related to other Tai languages. Khün shares 90% to 95% lexical similarity with Northern Thai language, 92% to 95% with Lü, 93% to 97% with Shan, and 80% to 83% with standard Thai. Tai Khun is traditionally written using a variant of the Tai Tham script.",Khün,Kra-Dai
6,"(Tai) Khün alphabet, pronunciation and language - Omniglot",https://www.omniglot.com/writing/khun.htm,"Khün (ᨴᩱ᩠ᨿᨡᩨ᩠ᨶ) Khün is a member of the southwesetern Tai branch of the Kra-Dai or Tai-Kaidai language family. It is spoken in mainly eastern Myanmar, and also in southern China, northern Laos and northern Thailand by about 116,880 people.",Khün,Kra-Dai
